a very disturbing bullying incident on a  school bus caught on video raises  troubling questions about how the driver  and the school district handled this  incident the video shows a little Texas  five-year-old girl being attacked by  other kids now the driver appears to do  nothing despite pleas from this little  girl as Omar Villafranca reports her mom  now once the driver fired the disturbing  video shows five-year-old Alexis  Billings getting assaulted by not one  but two bigger kids on a Dallas school  bus at multiple points during the attack  she called out for help but help never  came  I couldn't believe what I saw Alexis's  mother Audrey Billings says she is angry  the bus driver did not help the little  girl I couldn't believe that there was  an adult there that could have stopped  it he does nothing the five year olds  mother says she requested the video  after the girl told her two boys hit her  before the mom posted it online she says  she had to pay the school district $600  for a copy the incident happened last  November as the children were leaving  school in the video you can see Billings  daughter is seated a couple rows behind  the unidentified bus driver as she yells  for his help the driver did ask the  other child to stop but never physically  intervene  the mother says during the attack alexis  was stabbed with the pencil choked and  elbowed in the neck in all the abuse  lasted about 12 minutes  the driver was removed from that bus  route but Billings is demanding he be  fired he should not be driving children  he needs to be removed from that  position 100% the Dallas Independent  School District issued a statement  saying they've taken steps to ensure  student safety including more training  and monitoring according to a 2017  government study about one in four US  students say they have been bullied  Billings says her daughter no longer  takes the bus and she hopes what  happened to her daughter doesn't happen  to other children this is my one chance  to make a change and I need to make sure  that I take advantage of that for CBS  this morning  Omar Villafranca Dallas thanks to that  mother for speaking up listen it's not  even my child and it's tough watching  that why wouldn't you just pull over get  out of your seat and stop that yeah well  you need a standard to be in place  you
 

